 ### vtkImageSincInterpolator
-This class approximates sinc interpolation by multiplying the sinc function with a window function to limit kernel size [S1]. It supports the following window functions: Lanczos, Kaiser (adjustment parameter off), Cosine, Hann, Hamming, Blackman, and Nuttall [S1]. In Fourier space, the resolution of the spectral window is reduced to the order of the half-width of the sinc function [S1]. Consequently, the quality of sinc interpolation depends on both the window function type and the window half-width (WHW), which ranges from 1 to 16 [S1]. Additionally, it supports blur factors (BF) in x, y, and z directions to blur data during interpolation, which automatically increases the kernel size and computation time [S1].
